{"title":"1985 USAMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Notes\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Notes</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Determine each real root of\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/e/d5e92511bd4c69819499192dddd6e6e27e9e4aef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^4-(2\\cdot10^{10}+1)x^2-x+10^{20}+10^{10}-1=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"363\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>correct to four decimal places.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The equation can be re-written as \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/a/60aef22d5b804d3700eacd9cef9c8c7beb5af1e6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align}\\label{eqn1} (x+10^5)^2(x-10^5)^2 -(x+10^5)(x-10^5) -x-1=0. \\end{align}\" width=\"462\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>We first prove that the equation has no negative roots.\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bb5b28b20b09a51ff3a91e64ccbefb9750b7634.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\le 0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"47\" height=\"15\" /> The equation above can be further re-arranged as\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/1/a618d95d7158a1adc0db31b69a97179aaedcd37c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}[(x+10^5)(x-10^5)+1][(x+10^5)(x-10^5)-2]=x-1.\\end{align*}\" width=\"439\" height=\"20\" />\nThe right hand side of the equation is negative. Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/3/18363b75517e2085fdc92bff4b85190a5e8acef8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[(x+10^5)(x-10^5)+1][(x+10^5)(x-10^5)-2)]&lt;0,\\]\" width=\"414\" height=\"20\" /> and we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/6/1c6c8f00265fccdbfd056b81930c0bdcf8046ad9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1&lt;(x+10^5)(x-10^5) &lt;2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"229\" height=\"19\" /> Then the left hand side of the equation is bounded by\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/7/9b78e6f69f6767c2d95ea51df2dea9194bc1dc80.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|[(x+10^5)(x-10^5)+1][(x+10^5)(x-10^5)-2]|\\le 3\\times 3.\\]\" width=\"448\" height=\"20\" />\nHowever, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/3/1e37264606d4fd734e785ea8989ba33b957f0b28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|(x+10^5)(x-10^5)|\\le 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"187\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/c/8ec80ac1bb0dad8dfc650c262466c85e25ae382f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&lt;0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"47\" height=\"16\" /> it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/4/b14b9d449cec96db10ffb739ac98aee5f0886ecb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x+10^5| &lt;\\frac{2}{|x-10^5|}&lt;2\\times 10^{-5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"255\" height=\"41\" /> for negative <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/3/fc3be04db73828946870d3ccc6d122395a4bacf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/b/adba4856f67e6096aa08dd3b0c60ad36b3768e4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&lt;2\\times 10^{-5}-10^5.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"157\" height=\"18\" /> The right hand side of the equation is then a large negative number. It cannot be equal to the left hand side which is bounded by 9.\n</p><p>Now let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/b/acbc84e38fcf36b728033e68ab60cb4be6fee9d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/0/3b04c17c4de745d83ce0ac0183ddc21ba715b206.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=10^5,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" /> the left hand side of equation (1) is negative. Therefore the equation has real roots on both side of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/d/e7d8b576968ccdbfeff38053b7c606905adb945e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^5$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" />, as its leading coefficient is positive. We will prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/1/7d112306eae7f2d7ba493698fa072c2d469f4b8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=10^5$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" /> is a good approximation of the roots (within <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/9/cd90d7672d820e5cd0efca5adc18d8641439a1de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{-2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" />). In fact, we can solve the \"quadratic\" equation (1) for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/8/8b89bbac168079f8ea326048f2db256f6af48a3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x+10^5)(x-10^5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"143\" height=\"19\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/5/9b507444bb04d93f92306ab610d39176555b3e1b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x+10^5)(x-10^5)=\\frac{1\\pm\\sqrt{1+4(x+1)}}{2}.\\]\" width=\"320\" height=\"41\" />\nThen <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/6/366800cc1971a5ad9b7f2a0b3a31058af153c7dc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x-10^5=\\frac{1\\pm\\sqrt{1+4(x+1)}}{2(x+10^5)}.\\]\" width=\"235\" height=\"45\" />\nEasy to see that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/8/0c8598fcc5332d7abcccdd96c732f4cc2caa9bde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x-10^5| &lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"100\" height=\"19\" /> for positve <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/3/fc3be04db73828946870d3ccc6d122395a4bacf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/a/4ca53fa956e75403775eafdad3bab6df4ea75ab5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^5-1&lt;x&lt;10^5+1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"176\" height=\"16\" /> Then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/5/e85012b46b2746af3b926012014c1433f9622781.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} |x-10^5|&amp;=\\left|\\frac{1\\pm\\sqrt{1+4(x+1)}}{2(x+10^5)}\\right |\\\\ &amp;\\le \\left |\\frac{1}{2(x+10^5)}\\right |+\\left |\\frac{\\sqrt{1+4(x+1)}}{2(x+10^5)}\\right |\\\\ &amp;\\le \\frac{1}{2(10^5-1+10^5)} +\\frac{\\sqrt{1+4(10^5+1+1)}}{2(10^5-1+10^5)} \\\\ &amp;&lt;10^{-2}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"407\" height=\"188\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/ccada11db7b2b90693e2fac4f887a57fce6f96bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> be a root of the equation with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/5/f256ad90acf941652526341428235e4e34d3c749.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1&lt;10^5.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"71\" height=\"17\" /> Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/c/d4cdfc6e6b620a12d106e121e2d9944941af02e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;10^5-x_1&lt;10^{-2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"158\" height=\"17\" /> and \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/7/957007b680d69bcfbca76d5ed14317fad7fad2fa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_1-10^5=\\frac{1-\\sqrt{1+4(x_1+1)}}{2(x_1+10^5)}.\\]\" width=\"250\" height=\"45\" />\nAn aproximation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/ccada11db7b2b90693e2fac4f887a57fce6f96bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> is defined as follows:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/2/a624c9f92d28d9fe395d12e74c77f93ca682b0cf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\tilde{x}_1=10^5+\\frac{1-\\sqrt{1+4(10^5+1)}}{2(10^5+10^5)}.\\]\" width=\"257\" height=\"45\" />\nWe check the error of the estimate:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/7/9c73923e5ebe3c2d70fd1391378079690662ed33.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} |\\tilde{x}_1-x_1|&amp;=\\left | \\frac{1-\\sqrt{1+4(10^5+1)}}{2(10^5+10^5)}- \\frac{1-\\sqrt{1+4(x_1+1)}}{2(x_1+10^5)} \\right | \\\\ &amp;\\le \\left |\\frac{1}{2(10^5+10^5)}- \\frac{1}{2(x_1+10^5)}\\right |+\\left |\\frac{\\sqrt{1+4(10^5+1)}}{2(10^5+10^5)}- \\frac{\\sqrt{1+4(x_1+1)}}{2(x_1+10^5)}\\right |. \\end{align*}\" width=\"639\" height=\"114\" />\n</p><p>The first absolute value \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/e/b5e92299d05f59356dc1498f0471f6af0d5fb907.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left |\\frac{1}{2(10^5+10^5)}- \\frac{1}{2(x_1+10^5)}\\right | =\\frac{|x_1- 10^5|}{2(10^5+10^5)(x_1+10^5)}&lt;10^{-12}.\\]\" width=\"500\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>The second absolute value \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/4/9e4c160912f9d56a101a9908e6e00a2373ce0a91.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} &amp;\\left |\\frac{\\sqrt{1+4(10^5+1)}}{2(10^5+10^5)} - \\frac{\\sqrt{1+4(x_1+1)}}{2(x_1+10^5)} \\right |\\\\ &amp;\\le \\left |\\frac{\\sqrt{1+4(10^5+1)}}{2(10^5+10^5)}- \\frac{\\sqrt{1+4(x_1+1)}}{2(10^5+10^5)}\\right |+\\left |\\frac{\\sqrt{1+4(x_1+1)}}{2(10^5+10^5)}- \\frac{\\sqrt{1+4(x_1+1)}}{2(x_1+10^5)}\\right |\\\\ &amp;\\le 10^{-7}+10^{-9}, \\end{align*}\" width=\"616\" height=\"139\" />\nthrough a rationalized numerator.Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/7/f176d03ef82f9e0327f3fe7be3bc5bcf55d6a2ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|\\tilde{x}_1-x_1|\\le 10^{-6}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"132\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>For a real root <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7d010bbff66a0c41e43310a51efbaa6bf63396.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/7/487b2f775a1260ad9453aa7c02597eca6bec3a92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_2&gt;10^5,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" /> we choose \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/c/02ce86d09ecd40d14105a055b20aed6c74486cef.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\tilde{x}_2=10^5+\\frac{1+\\sqrt{1+4(10^5+1)}}{2(10^5+10^5)}.\\]\" width=\"257\" height=\"45\" />\nWe can similarly prove it has the desired approximation.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notes\">Notes</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Notes\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Another round of iteration can increase the accuracy to more than 10 decimal places:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/4/004bf13708fdb30c9c10e169401ca106e96adb08.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\tilde{x}_1^\\prime=10^5+\\frac{1-\\sqrt{1+4(\\tilde{x}_1+1)}}{2(\\tilde{x}_1+10^5)},\\\\ \\tilde{x}_2^\\prime=10^5+\\frac{1+\\sqrt{1+4(\\tilde{x}_2+1)}}{2(\\tilde{x}_2+10^5)}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"250\" height=\"98\" />\n</p><p>J.Z.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_USAMO\" title=\"1985 USAMO\">1985 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"1985 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1985\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1985 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1985 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1985 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1985 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1985 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1985 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017163047\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.032 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.051 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 235/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1267/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8330/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.527      1 -total\n 55.61%    6.966      1 Template:USAMO_box\n 42.63%    5.341      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:15076:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017163047 and revision id 94593. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}